// Nothing below is a gap to be filled by hand: a hand-written `@FFI.Extern`
// for one of these would be refused by the same rule that skipped it.
// WGPUDawnCacheDeviceDescriptor: `WGPUDawnCacheDeviceDescriptor`, whose field `dawnLoadCacheDataCallbackInfo` is `WGPUDawnLoadCacheDataCallbackInfo`, whose field `callback` is a pointer to `const unsigned char`, which has no name to point at
// WGPUDawnLoadCacheDataCallbackInfo: `WGPUDawnLoadCacheDataCallbackInfo`, whose field `callback` is a pointer to `const unsigned char`, which has no name to point at
// WGPUDawnStoreCacheDataCallbackInfo: `WGPUDawnStoreCacheDataCallbackInfo`, whose field `callback` is a pointer to `const unsigned char`, which has no name to point at
// WGPUDawnTogglesDescriptor: `WGPUDawnTogglesDescriptor`, whose field `enabledToggles` is a pointer to `const char *const`, which has no name to point at
// WGPUDawnWGSLBlocklist: `WGPUDawnWGSLBlocklist`, whose field `blocklistedFeatures` is a pointer to `const char *const`, which has no name to point at
// WGPUDeviceDescriptor: `WGPUDeviceDescriptor`, whose field `deviceLostCallbackInfo` is `WGPUDeviceLostCallbackInfo`, whose field `callback` is a pointer to `struct WGPUDeviceImpl *const`, which has no name to point at
// WGPUDeviceLostCallbackInfo: `WGPUDeviceLostCallbackInfo`, whose field `callback` is a pointer to `struct WGPUDeviceImpl *const`, which has no name to point at
